Compatibility with bsl-language-server
--------------------------------------
Where this project reports the same diagnostics as bsl-language-server,
the agreement is deliberate. Rule codes, tags, severities, default
activation and the places a rule fires form an interface that existing
SonarQube quality profiles and CI pipelines depend on; a tool that
reported different rules under different names on the same code would
not replace its predecessor. These values match that project's published
rule documentation, which is where they can be checked.

This is a statement about observable behaviour, not about source code:
implementing the same interface independently is intended, and copying
implementation text is not.

1C platform help data
---------------------
bsl-analyzer no longer bundles 1C platform help. Until issue #312 the file
crates/bsl-platform/data/platform_data.json — a structured extract of the
1C:Enterprise context-help archives (shcntx_ru.hbk, shlang_ru.hbk) — was
bundled; it is removed from the tree and from builds, and remains only in
the history. The help is now read at runtime from the user's installed
platform or from a separately distributed help package
(docs/configuration/PROJECT_CONFIGURATION.md, [platform_help]); with no
platform installed, the default `auto` source serves the built-in
interface facts; a corpus with descriptions is configured explicitly.

The contents of that corpus and of every help package — in particular
method descriptions, parameter documentation and code examples — are
© ООО «1С-Софт» and are NOT covered by the project's MIT license. A help package carries its own NOTICE.md with that
statement; its use is on the practical assumption that it serves
interoperability with the 1C platform rather than a standalone
documentation product. See crates/bsl-platform/data/PROVENANCE.md for the
history and the full statement.

